<title>USA: Duke S.C. Catawba 1 nuke at full power.</title>
<headline>Duke S.C. Catawba 1 nuke at full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1,129 megawatt (MW) Catawba 1 nuclear unit in Clover, S.C., is again operating at full power following Monday's outage, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Thursday.</p>
<p>Monday's outage was caused by a relay failure in the reactor protection control system while operators were doing routine tests, Duke Power Co, the plant's operator said earlier this week.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, is operating at full power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
